  "description": "Overview Understand. Simulate. Build. Debug. Circuit Debugging is a three-round technical event of Addovedi 2026 (NIT Arunachal Pradesh) that goes from theory, to simulation, to real hardware debugging . Observe. Measure. Diagnose. Repair. Verify. Held on campus, 28-30 October 2026 . Guidelines Eligibility: college students, valid college ID required. Team size: up to 2 members (solo also fine). Inter-college / inter-specialization: allowed. Open to all branches. Rounds: 3. Quiz, LTspice simulation, breadboard debugging. Duration: Round 1 is 20 minutes. Rounds 2 and 3 limits announced before the round. Scoring: 100 marks (30 + 30 + 40). Final rank is the combined score. Bring: your own laptop with LTspice installed and tested. Organisers provide components and instruments. Registration: sign up on the Addovedi website, register for Circuit Debugging to get your Team ID, then register on Unstop with the Team ID + the leader's Addovedi ID. Registration fee: Rs. 50 per member (each team member pays Rs. 50). Prize pool: Rs. 13,000+ (including goodies). Rules Report before the reporting time with a valid ID card. LTspice must be ready beforehand. Organisers aren't responsible for laptop or software delays. In Round 3, diagnose before replacing . Random replacement isn't valid debugging. Use equipment carefully . No damage or misuse. Don't interfere with other teams. You may be asked to explain your work . Organisers may inspect files and circuits. Unfair means or cheating = disqualification. Organisers may change sequence or qualification criteria and will announce it. Judges' and coordinators' decisions are final.",
