    "details": "<p><strong>Overview</strong></p>\n<p><em>Understand. Simulate. Build. Debug.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Circuit Debugging</strong>&nbsp;is a&nbsp;<strong>three-round technical event</strong>&nbsp;of Addovedi 2026 (NIT Arunachal Pradesh) that goes from&nbsp;<strong>theory, to simulation, to real hardware debugging</strong>. Observe. Measure. Diagnose. Repair. Verify. Held on campus,&nbsp;<strong>28-30 October 2026</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Guidelines</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Eligibility:&nbsp;college students, valid&nbsp;college ID&nbsp;required.</li>\n<li>Team size:&nbsp;up to 2 members&nbsp;(solo also fine).</li>\n<li>Inter-college / inter-specialization:&nbsp;allowed. Open to all branches.</li>\n<li>Rounds:&nbsp;3. Quiz, LTspice simulation, breadboard debugging.</li>\n<li>Duration:&nbsp;Round 1 is&nbsp;20 minutes. Rounds 2 and 3 limits announced before the round.</li>\n<li>Scoring:&nbsp;100 marks&nbsp;(30 + 30 + 40). Final rank is the&nbsp;combined score.</li>\n<li>Bring:&nbsp;your&nbsp;own laptop with LTspice installed and tested. Organisers provide components and instruments.</li>\n<li>Registration:&nbsp;sign up on the Addovedi website, register for Circuit Debugging to get your&nbsp;Team ID, then register on Unstop with the&nbsp;Team ID + the leader's Addovedi ID.</li>\n<li>Registration fee:&nbsp;Rs. 50 per member&nbsp;(each team member pays Rs. 50).</li>\n<li>Prize pool:&nbsp;Rs. 13,000+&nbsp;(including goodies).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Report before the reporting time</strong>&nbsp;with a valid ID card.</li>\n<li><strong>LTspice must be ready beforehand.</strong>&nbsp;Organisers aren't responsible for laptop or software delays.</li>\n<li>In Round 3,&nbsp;<strong>diagnose before replacing</strong>. Random replacement isn't valid debugging.</li>\n<li>Use equipment&nbsp;<strong>carefully</strong>.&nbsp;<strong>No damage or misuse.</strong>&nbsp;Don't interfere with other teams.</li>\n<li>You may be asked to&nbsp;<strong>explain your work</strong>. Organisers may inspect files and circuits.</li>\n<li><strong>Unfair means or cheating = disqualification.</strong></li>\n<li>Organisers may change sequence or qualification criteria and will announce it.</li>\n<li><strong>Judges' and coordinators' decisions are final.</strong></li>\n</ul>",
